; Regression (2026-09-23): a `{` block on the same line as an `if` condition.
; An Expression may be a Block, so `if k = 1 { return 10 }` parsed the block as
; the condition's LAST OPERAND, the line break ended the condition, and the
; NEXT statement became the body: the block never ran and the tail value after
; it was swallowed — this function answered 0 for every k at rc 0 (tscaly
; lessons §3.5ji: 237 printer dispatch arms fell through). The same holds for
; while/for/choose/match; the block belongs on a line of its own.
; xfail: error: a block on the same line as the if condition is read as part of the condition
function one_line(k: int) returns int
{
    if k = 1 { return 10 }
    20
}

print "`one_line(1)`\n"
